<article class="env-lemma" id="0FGX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FGX">Lemma <span data-tag="0FGX">45.7.5</span>.</a> Let $H^*$ be a classical Weil cohomology theory (Definition <a href="/tag/0FGV" data-tag="0FGV">45.7.3</a>). Let $X$ and $Y$ be smooth projective varieties. Then $\int _{X \times Y} = \int _ X \otimes \int _ Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Say $\dim (X) = d$ and $\dim (Y) = e$. By axiom (B) we have $H^{2d + 2e}(X \times Y) = H^{2d}(X) \otimes H^{2e}(Y)$ and by axiom (A)(d) this is $1$-dimensional. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0FGW" data-tag="0FGW">45.7.4</a> this $1$-dimensional vector space generated by the class $\gamma ([x \times y])$ of a closed point $(x, y)$ and $\int _{X \times Y} \gamma ([x \times y]) = 1$. Since $\gamma ([x \times y]) = \gamma ([x]) \otimes \gamma ([y])$ by axioms (C)(a) and (C)(c) and since $\int _ X \gamma ([x]) = 1$ and $\int _ Y \gamma ([y]) = 1$ we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>